# Component Rules

## Required Structure for Every Component

```tsx
"use client";
import type React from "react";
// ... other imports

const MyComponent: React.FC<MyComponentProps> = ({ prop = default }) => {
  // All hooks FIRST — before any early returns
  const [state, setState] = useState(false);
  const computed = useMemo(() => ..., [deps]);

  // Early returns after all hooks
  if (!data) return null;

  return <div>...</div>;
};

export default MyComponent;
```

## Generic Table Components
Use `<T>` generic for all data-typed components:
```tsx
const TableComponent = <T,>({ data, props }: TableProps<T>) => { ... };
```

## Styling Pattern
Always merge default + custom class names using the `disableDefaultStyles` guard:
```tsx
const containerClass = disableDefaultStyles
  ? customClassNames.container || ""
  : `rtbl-container ${customClassNames.container || ""}`;
```
Never hardcode colors inline — use Tailwind utilities or `rtbl-*` CSS classes.

## Dark Mode
Detect via `window.matchMedia("(prefers-color-scheme: dark)")` inside a `useEffect`.
Pass `isDarkMode` state to conditionally apply Tailwind dark classes (`bg-gray-900`, etc.).
Apply `dark` class to `rtbl-container` so CSS dark variants activate: `${isDarkMode ? "dark" : ""}`.

## Accessibility
- Every interactive element needs `role`, `tabIndex`, and `onKeyDown` (Enter key at minimum)
- Action buttons: `aria-label`, `type="button"`
- Loading states: `aria-busy="true"`, `aria-live="polite"`, `role="status"`
- Tables: use `scope="col"` on `<th>`, `<span className="sr-only">` for screen-reader-only text

## Portal Usage (ActionDropdown)
The action dropdown uses `createPortal(menu, document.body)` to escape table overflow clipping.
Position is computed from `buttonRef.current.getBoundingClientRect()` on open.
Always clean up event listeners in `useEffect` return.

## Props Interface Location
All interfaces go in `src/types/index.ts`, NOT inline in the component file.
